          "model": "openai/gpt-5.4",
          "type": "ai_answer",
          "text": "It means: **for GLUE, BERT turns the whole input into one summary vector and puts a simple classifier on top of it.**\n\n- **Input format:** Put in either one sentence or a sentence pair using BERT’s normal format from Section 3.\n- **Use `[CLS]`:** After the input passes through BERT, take the final hidden state of the first token, `[CLS]`. That vector is \\(C \\in \\mathbb{R}^H\\), and it is treated as the summary of the whole example.\n- **Add a classifier:** Learn a matrix \\(W \\in \\mathbb{R}^{K \\times H}\\), where \\(K\\) is the number of possible labels and \\(H\\) is BERT’s hidden size.\n- **Make predictions:** Compute scores for each label with\n  \\[\n  CW^T\n  \\]\n  then apply **softmax** to turn those scores into probabilities.\n- **Train with classification loss:** Compare those probabilities to the true label using standard log-likelihood / cross-entropy loss.\n\nIn plain English: **BERT reads the text, `[CLS]` becomes the “summary embedding,” and one small linear layer decides the label.**",
